-- title:
--   Unique lifting to a local ring with nilpotent maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be a Noetherian commutative local ring and let $D$ be a commutative local ring equipped with a $V$-algebra structure whose structure map $V \to D$ is a local homomorphism and makes $D$ a flat $V$-module, subject to the hypothesis $\mathfrak m_V D = \mathfrak m_D$ (the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_V$ equals $\mathfrak m_D$), and assume the residue field extension $\kappa(D)/\kappa(V)$ is finite and separable. Let $T$ be a further commutative local $V$-algebra whose maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_T$ is nilpotent, i.e. $\mathfrak m_T^N = 0$ for some $N$. Let $\iota \colon \kappa(D) \to \kappa(T)$ be a ring homomorphism that is compatible with $V$ in the sense that for every $v \in V$ one has $\iota(\overline{v_D}) = \overline{v_T}$, where $v_D$ and $v_T$ denote the images of $v$ in $D$ and in $T$ and the bars are the residue maps. Then there is exactly one $V$-algebra homomorphism $g \colon D \to T$ with $\overline{g(d)} = \iota(\bar d)$ in $\kappa(T)$ for all $d \in D$.
--
--   This is the level-by-level (Artinian target) form of the unramified lifting statement for local algebras: a prescribed residue-field homomorphism extends uniquely to a $V$-algebra map, as in the classical theory of formally étale extensions. It is the input for the corresponding statement over an adically complete target, obtained by passing to the limit over the quotients $T = E/\mathfrak m_E^m$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_existsUnique_algHom_residue_eq_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_isNilpotent_maximalIdeal.lean

